  clock: 1  # 6e02
  nonce: '6e02'  # 6e02
  data:  # 6e02
    kind: work_item  # 6e02
    title: "ADR-0017 §4a inferred summaries have zero production callers and the dataclass lacks param_to_calls — the field that lifts the cross_function blocker (76.3% of never-ran walks)"  # 6e02
    status: todo_hard  # 6e02
    priority: 1  # 6e02
    parent:  # 6e02
    tags:  # 6e02
    - taint  # 6e02
    - dataflow  # 6e02
    - adr_0017  # 6e02
    isbefore: []  # 6e02
    duplicate_of: []  # 6e02
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 6e02
    pr_ref:  # 6e02
    description: "ADR-0017 §3a step 3 says \"At call sites, apply function summaries (§4)\". Half of\n§4 is live; the half that lifts the dominant blocker does not exist.\n\nVERIFIED IN THE CODE 2026-08-26 on dev daafb0abb1, not taken from WI-kabif's\ntally (which records blocker 5 \"§4 function summaries\" as DONE (#197) -- true of\n§4b only):\n\n  §4b DECLARED summaries      LIVE. propagate_taint_ddg calls\n                              load_function_summaries() (taint.py:3363-3364);\n                              38 terminating entries feed _use_site_terminates\n                              (taint.py:3059, 3075, def at 3134).\n  §4a INFERRED summaries      ZERO production callers. infer_summary is\n                              implemented (function_summaries/__init__.py:196)\n                              and called only from tests.\n\nAND THE SHIPPED DATACLASS IS MISSING THREE OF THE FIVE FIELDS §4a SPECIFIES.\nRepo-wide grep: `CallArgFlow`, `param_to_calls`, `param_to_param` appear ONLY in\ndocs/adr/0017-taint-zone-dataflow.md. They exist nowhere in packages/.\n\n  ADR §4a field          shipped?\n  symbol_id              NO  (dataclass keys on `function`, a name string)\n  param_to_return        YES\n  param_to_param         NO  -- and §4a says of it, verbatim, \"**param_to_param\n                             is not deferred.**\" The dataclass has param_to_self\n                             + mutates_self instead, which is the receiver case\n                             only, not param N -> out-param M.\n  param_to_calls         NO  -- THIS IS THE ONE THAT MATTERS (see below)\n  return_sources         COMPUTED AND DISCARDED. infer_summary builds the list\n                             at __init__.py:241/247 and its return statement\n                             (:249) omits it, so the value is thrown away.\n\nWHY param_to_calls IS THE GATE. It answers \"does param N flow to an argument of\na call to F?\" -- exactly the fact needed to carry taint across a call boundary.\nWithout it the §3a walk cannot even attempt a flow whose source and sink sit in\ndifferent functions, and it does not try:\n\n    taint.py:3541-3543\n      elif sink_node != source_fn:\n          # §3a is intraprocedural by construction. ... it is the\n          # blocker §4 function summaries exist to lift.\n          blocked_by = WALK_BLOCKED_CROSS_FUNCTION\n\nMEASURED SIZE (docs/measurements/0007, 11 repos, 298 rows). Of the 139\nddg_mixed rows whose walk NEVER RAN: cross_function 106 (76.3%),\nsource_not_tracked 24 (17.3%), sink_before_source 9 (6.5%).\n\nTHESE PARTITION -- THEY DO NOT ADD, and this is the trap to avoid pricing into\nthe payoff. The three blockers are successive `elif` branches over the same rows\n(taint.py:3536-3546), so a row reading cross_function today may simply RELABEL to\nthe next blocker once composition lands rather than becoming a walk. The yield is\nstrictly under 106 and is currently unmeasured. Measuring it is step 1 below, not\nan afterthought.\n\nSTEP 1 IS PRICING, NOT BUILDING (L3: price the ceiling before building it).\nInstrument the cross_function bail to record, per blocked row, whether a\nSINGLE-HOP composition could connect it: the tainted value is an argument at a\ncall from source_fn to sink_node, and sink_node has DDG. No behaviour change, no\nremoval authority, both arms of WI-kabif's ceiling instrument already exist\n(p4_busis_08252026/measure-refutation-payoff.py).\n\nPRE-REGISTERED EXPECTATION, written before the instrument runs so it can be\nscored, and following this item's parent in making the tripwire explicit:\n  * Of the 106 cross_function rows, 25-50% become walks that actually RUN\n    (produce confirmed / unconfirmed / escaped), central estimate 35%.\n  * The rest relabel, dominated by source_not_tracked -- because the same\n    receiver/def-tracking gap that produces today's 17.3% applies to the callee's\n    parameter binding.\n  * The UNCONFIRMED population -- the ONLY one §7a removal could ever act on with\n    evidence, and ZERO in every repo today -- stays under 15% of newly-running\n    walks.\n  IF THE MEASUREMENT REPORTS A MUCH LARGER NUMBER, SUSPECT THE MEASUREMENT. That\n  rule is what caught the +6.3pt error on WI-kabif (26.8% vs a filed 18%), and it\n  is repeated here deliberately rather than assumed inherited.\n\nSAFETY DIRECTION IS FAVOURABLE, AND WORTH STATING BECAUSE THE PARENT'S IS NOT.\n§3a is CONFIRM-ONLY: the walk raises confidence and never removes a flow\n(taint.py docstring, ~:2866). So landing composition ADDS confirmations and can\nonly make labels more precise. Removal authority stays WI-kabif's and stays\nbehind INV-busis. The container/alias FALSE-NEGATIVE trade WI-kabif owns in\nwriting is NOT incurred by this item -- but note PR #214's sanitizer barrier is\na second consumer of the walk's False, so any change here must state which\ndirection it moves False (INV-lupav's forfeit_refutation gate applies).\n\nDOCS DEFECT FOUND WHILE FILING, small and separable: ADR-0017's top-of-file\nStatus line still reads \"§4 function summaries and §7a field-sensitivity are\nSPECIFIED BUT NOT IMPLEMENTED -- each has no production consumer (measured\n2026-08-02)\". §4b has had a production consumer since #197 (2026-08-04).\ntaint.py's own docstring already corrects that exact sentence in place (\"THAT\nPARAGRAPH USED TO END ... Half of it is now false and it was load-bearing\"); the\nADR header never received the same edit. Fix the Status line to split §4a from\n§4b when this item lands."  # 6e02
    fields: {}  # 6e02
