    isbefore: [WI-kabif-dahad-kufuz-vodoz-misaj-batut-honab-nizib]  # b982
    not_duplicate_of: [WI-sivuz-bahuv-halug-jitaf-jubuj-fokug-livaf-dupod, WI-variv-lujug-fobig-nojit-piraz-lojam-lizil-dosip]  # b982
- op: discuss  # bd26
  at: '2026-08-26T16:26:02Z'  # bd26
  by: agent  # bd26
  actor: jgstern_agent  # bd26
  clock: 3  # bd26
  nonce: bd26  # bd26
  message: "STEP 1 (PRICING) IS DONE. Measurement 0008; instrument\nscripts/measure-cross-function-reach.py; raw in\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p5_famig_08262026/json/.\n\nTHE CEILING: 18.3% of cross-function findings (778 of 4,245) meet the NECESSARY\nconditions for a single-hop composed walk -- source function calls the sink's\nfunction directly, and the sink's function carries reaching-def coverage.\nPer-repository median 22.3%, range 0%-100%. Sufficiency additionally needs the\ntainted value to be an ARGUMENT at the call, which is param_to_calls and does not\nexist, so this is a ceiling and the achievable figure is strictly below it.\n\nPER-REPO, because the pooled figure is a beads statistic wearing a cohort's name\n(beads alone is 62.4% of pooled findings -- INV-duvup):\n\n  repo             xf find   1hop+ddg   ceiling\n  ArkLib                 8          8    100.0%\n  beads               2650        565     21.3%\n  cert-manager          30         11     36.7%\n  cilium               953         76      8.0%\n  gocryptfs            400         93     23.2%\n  jaeger                58         20     34.5%\n  kamaraflow             0          -   EXCLUDED  (0 xf findings; all 6 blocked\n                                                   walks stop at\n                                                   source_not_tracked, so its\n                                                   zero measures a DIFFERENT\n                                                   blocker)\n  mobx                   2          0      0.0%\n  plausible              7          5     71.4%\n  session-desktop        7          0      0.0%\n  spacedrive           130          0      0.0%\n  POOLED              4245        778     18.3%\n\n*** THE RESULT THAT DECIDES THIS ITEM, AND IT IS NOT THE CEILING. *** The payoff\nsplits by DIRECTION, and the two halves want different decisions:\n\n  REFUTATION: BOUNDED AT ZERO, AND COMPOSITION DOES NOT MOVE IT. Removal\n  authority can act only on `unconfirmed` -- the walk ran and established no\n  dependence. Over the same 11 repositories, of the 28 walks that RAN:\n  14 confirmed / 14 escaped / ZERO unconfirmed. Composition manufactures running\n  walks; on the observed split those become confirmations and escapes, not the\n  class removal needs. So §4a is NOT the gate on WI-kabif's removal arm that\n  0007's framing implied, and this item should not be sold as unblocking it.\n\n  CONFIRMATION: REAL, AND IT INFLATES THE OUTPUT -- a cost nobody had priced.\n  `analysis_method` is IN the collapse key and adjudicated flows bypass\n  collapse_unadjudicated_flows entirely (taint.py:641). So a newly-confirmed flow\n  becomes ITS OWN ROW while the ddg_mixed group it left behind survives one\n  member lighter. A situation of 40 members with 10 confirmations becomes ELEVEN\n  rows, not one improved one. At the ceiling that is up to 778 new `precise` rows\n  on a cohort that emits 298 rows in total.\n\nDEPTH IS NOT HEADROOM. Only 21.9% of cross-function findings are one hop. The\n56.4% \"whole chain covered\" figure should NOT be pursued: jaeger's 5-hop route\nruns from a _test.go helper through internal/tenancy into examples/hotrod, which\nis not plausibly a real call chain, and each extra hop multiplies exposure to\ncall-graph false edges. Composing along long routes would carry taint down\nfabricated paths.\n\nLANGUAGE: go is 94.2% of findings (ceiling 18.2%), so this cohort is\nsubstantially a Go measurement. python 46.3% and javascript 45.8% are more than\ndouble it on volumes too small to carry weight. rust (130 findings) and\ntypescript (9) return a STRUCTURAL ZERO -- rust has none at one hop and none with\na fully-covered route despite 82 with a covered sink.\n\nTHREE INDEPENDENT RECONCILIATIONS AGAINST 0007, which is why I believe the\ninstrument rather than merely its output: (1) cross-function evidence rows total\n106 against 0007's independently-reported 106; (2) the verdict census reproduces\n0007's result table ROW FOR ROW (14/0/14/139/131, 298 rows); (3) per repository\nthe blockers reconcile to 0007's not_attempted column (beads 58+16=74,\njaeger 9+2=11, ...).\n\nPRE-REGISTRATION SCORED, and it scored badly. Predicted 25-50% (central 35%) of\ncross-function rows becoming running walks. The single-hop ceiling is 18.3%\n(BELOW the band); the all-hops ceiling is 56.4% (above it). THE PRE-REGISTRATION\nWAS UNDERSPECIFIED -- it never named a composition DEPTH, so it does not\nadjudicate between them. Its own invalidation section says \"the 1-hop figure is\nthe one to trust\", and under that reading the prediction was too optimistic. The\ntripwire (suspect a much LARGER number) did NOT fire; the number is smaller, in\nthe direction of less payoff, and three reconciliations corroborate the\npopulation.\n\nWHAT STEPS 2-3 SHOULD NOW BE. NOT \"build param_to_calls to unblock removal\" --\nthat is refuted above. If §4a is built at all it is a LABELLING change, and it\nmust be priced against the row-inflation cost before, not after. The single\nnumber most worth re-checking first is the 0-of-28 unconfirmed rate: it is\nconsistent across every repository and across 0007's independent run, but 28\nwalks is a small base, and \"unconfirmed is 0 among walks that run today\" is not\nthe same claim as \"unconfirmed would be ~0 among walks composition makes run\".\nThat inference is the load-bearing one and it is NOT measured."  # bd26
- op: discuss  # 2449
  at: '2026-08-30T10:24:05Z'  # 2449
  by: agent  # 2449
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2449
  clock: 4  # 2449
  nonce: '2449'  # 2449
  message: "THE SEPARABLE DOCS DEFECT THIS ITEM NAMES IS ALREADY CLOSED -- verified, not assumed. The description ends with: 'DOCS DEFECT FOUND WHILE FILING ... ADR-0017's top-of-file Status line still reads \"§4 function summaries and §7a field-sensitivity are SPECIFIED BUT NOT IMPLEMENTED\" ... Fix the Status line to split §4a from §4b when this item lands.'\n\nRead at dev 57af2cc060 today, docs/adr/0017-taint-zone-dataflow.md line 5: the Status line was re-measured 2026-08-26 on dev daafb0abb1 and now splits them exactly as asked -- '§4b declared summaries LIVE (declared terminating entries reach _use_site_terminates ...)' against '§4a inferred summaries IMPLEMENTED BUT UNWIRED (infer_summary, zero production callers -- and the shipped dataclass lacks the param_to_calls / param_to_param this subsection specifies, WI-famig)'. It also does the thing this item asked for and more: it names the distinction in terms ('\"Not implemented\" tells a reader to WRITE it; \"implemented but unwired\" tells them to WIRE it -- those are different jobs'), and it declines to pin a §4b count because the catalogue size moved 33 -> 108 -> 113 in two days.\n\nSo that line of work carries INV-lataj's fix, filed and landed independently of this item on the same day this item was filed. NOTHING IS OWED HERE. Removing it from the item's tail so the next reader does not spend the trip.\n\nThe item's remaining scope is unchanged and is NOT an implementation: step 1 (pricing) shipped as measurement 0008, its conclusion refuted 'build param_to_calls to unblock removal', and the load-bearing unmeasured claim it names for itself -- that unconfirmed would stay ~0 among walks composition MAKES run, inferred from 0-of-28 among walks that run today -- still stands unmeasured, and measuring it requires the composition prototype the item says should not be built before the row-inflation cost is priced. That ordering is a decision, not a next step."  # 2449
- op: discuss  # 6fd0
  at: '2026-09-02T02:33:24Z'  # 6fd0
  by: agent  # 6fd0
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 6fd0
  clock: 5  # 6fd0
  nonce: 6fd0  # 6fd0
  message: "STEP 2 (PRICING THE ROW-INFLATION COST) IS DONE, and it breaks the ordering\ndeadlock this item's last note recorded. Measurement 0011; instrument\nscripts/measure-row-inflation.py; raw in\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p6_famig_09012026/json/. Shipped as dev c05d573e69.\n\nTHE PRICE. At the composition ceiling the 11-repo cohort's EMITTED ROWS go\n3,166 -> 4,470: +1,304, x1.41. At 50% sufficiency x1.22, at 25% x1.11.\nReported as a curve, not a point, because sufficiency needs param_to_calls and\nthat does not exist. The hypothetical is deliberately GENEROUS to §4a -- it\nassumes every composable finding that composes is CONFIRMED, where 0008's split\nsays a running walk is as likely to escape, and an escaped walk stays\nddg_mixed. So the true cost at any rate is at most this and probably near half.\n\n*** THREE RESULTS MATTER MORE THAN THE HEADLINE ***\n\n(1) 0008'S RELATIVE FRAMING USED THE WRONG DENOMINATOR, and the correction goes\nthe reassuring way. 0008 wrote \"up to 778 new precise rows on a cohort that\nemits 298 rows in total\", which reads as ~x3.6. But 298 is measurement 0007's\ncount of rows CARRYING A WALK VERDICT, not the cohort's emitted rows, which are\n3,166. The absolute count was the right order; the ratio was overstated ~2.5x.\n\n(2) THE COST IS NOT ONE ROW PER CONFIRMATION. 1,549 composable findings yield\n+1,304 rows, not +1,549, because a group whose members are ALL composable\nVANISHES rather than surviving one member lighter. 783 of 2,977 groups are\ntouched and their sizes run 1..104 (125 have >=10 members; the eight largest\ncarry 52/54/57/58/81/86/88/94/104). A promotion out of a 104-member group costs\none row and leaves the group standing; out of a singleton it costs nothing.\nAny estimate that multiplies confirmations by one row is wrong in BOTH\ndirections at once.\n\n(3) *** THE RESULT THAT CHANGES WHAT THE DECISION IS. *** §4a would invalidate\na premise the collapse design states QUANTITATIVELY.\ncollapse_unadjudicated_flows' docstring justifies letting `ddg` bypass collapse\nbecause ddg \"is 6 of 359 census flows\" -- 1.7% -- so \"collapsing it would trade\nearned precision for 1.7% of the noise\". That premise REPRODUCES TODAY at\n1.43% (189 of 13,199 findings). At the ceiling composition takes it to 13.17%,\na 9x increase. The argument for the bypass is a claim about a proportion, and\n§4a moves the proportion. So §4a and the COLLAPSE KEY cannot be decided\nseparately -- which was not on the table before this measurement.\n\nCONTROL, because a model of collapse that merely looks right is the failure\nmode here. The instrument pools findings globally while verify-claims calls\ncollapse_unadjudicated_flows 2-4 times on DISJOINT subsets; a group straddling\na call boundary would under-count rows and OVERSTATE inflation. Spied on the\nproduction function: jaeger 290->133, gocryptfs 745->119, cert-manager 82->32,\nArkLib 15->6 -- exact on all four, including the repo with the largest\ninflation ratio (gocryptfs x1.92). The pooling assumption is validated, not\nassumed.\n\n0008'S CEILING HAS DRIFTED AND ITS PER-REPO TABLE IS STALE: pooled 18.3% ->\n14.8% in six days. Cross-function findings grew 2.5x (4,245 -> 10,445) while\nthe composable subset grew 2.0x. Five repositories are byte-identical (ArkLib,\nplausible, session-desktop, mobx, and kamaraflow's EXCLUDED control); five\nmoved (beads 2.1x, cilium 4.0x, jaeger 3.4x, gocryptfs 1.6x, cert-manager\n1.7x), and JAEGER'S CEILING HALVED, 34.5% -> 15.8%. Not a defect -- six days\nof taint and analyzer work landing -- but a ceiling quoted from 0008 today\nwould be wrong by 3.5 points. The SHAPE is informative: findings grew far\nfaster than rows (jaeger 111 -> 290 findings against 24 -> 26 walk-verdict\nrows). Collapse absorbed almost all of it, which is this record's own\nmechanism seen from the other side.\n\nPER-REPO, because pooling is a choice and the pooled figure is a beads\nstatistic (beads = 53% of findings, 73% of the composable set):\n\n  repo             rows now  composable  ceiling   rows @r=1   x\n  beads                2024        1138    20.6%        2979   1.47\n  cilium                606         221     5.8%         803   1.32\n  jaeger                133          31    15.8%         150   1.13\n  gocryptfs             119         127    19.6%         229   1.92\n  plausible             102           5    71.4%         104   1.02\n  spacedrive            101           0     0.0%         101   1.00\n  cert-manager           32          19    37.3%          49   1.53\n  mobx                   22           0     0.0%          22   1.00\n  session-desktop        21           0     0.0%          21   1.00\n  ArkLib                  6           8   100.0%          12   2.00\n  POOLED               3166        1549    14.8%        4470   1.41\n  kamaraflow          EXCLUDED (0 cross_function findings; its zero measures a\n                      different blocker -- same control 0008 applied)\n\nThe price is ANTI-CORRELATED WITH SIZE: the repos that dominate the finding\ncount inflate least proportionally, the smallest inflates most.\n\nWHAT IS STILL NOT MEASURED, unchanged and stated so it is not mistaken for\nresolved: whether `unconfirmed` would stay ~0 among walks composition MAKES\nrun. That still needs a prototype. What this measurement removes is the stated\nREASON not to build one.\n\nTHE DECISION IS NOW THREE OPTIONS, NOT TWO, and it is the owner's:\n  1. Build §4a and accept x1.11-x1.41. More rows, each more precise.\n  2. Build §4a AND revisit the `ddg` bypass so a composed confirmation collapses\n     with its siblings and carries the confirmation as a FIELD. Cheaper in rows,\n     and it re-opens a ruling INV-karud settled on a premise that no longer\n     holds at 13%.\n  3. Do not build §4a. Refutation payoff is bounded at zero (0008) and\n     confirmation is a labelling improvement on at most 14.8% of cross-function\n     findings.\nI am not choosing between these: (2) re-opens a ratified INV-karud ruling, and\n(1) vs (3) is a judgement about what the output is FOR -- 1,304 rows each\ncarrying a confirmed data dependence may well be worth more than the collapsed\nrows they left, and that is not a question a measurement answers."  # 6fd0
