  by: agent  # a8b2
  actor: jgstern_agent  # a8b2
  clock: 7  # a8b2
  nonce: a8b2  # a8b2
  message: "Status moved todo_hard -> needs_human_review because what remains is a DECISION, not work. Step 1 (pricing the ceiling) shipped as measurement 0008; step 2 (pricing the row cost) shipped today as measurement 0011, dev c05d573e69. The ordering deadlock this item recorded -- 'measuring the load-bearing claim requires the prototype, and the prototype must not be built before the row cost is priced' -- is now broken in the only direction a measurement can break it: the cost is priced, so the stated reason not to build the prototype is gone.\n\nWhat blocks is the three-way choice in the note above, and two of the three are not mine to make. Option 2 re-opens an INV-karud ruling that was ratified on a premise (ddg is 1.7% of flows) which this measurement shows composition moves to 13.17%. Option 1 vs option 3 is a judgement about what the output is FOR, not a fact about it -- x1.11 to x1.41 more rows, each carrying a confirmed data dependence rather than a collapsed group.\n\nNothing is owed on the implementation side until that is answered. If the answer is option 3 (do not build), this item closes wont_do with two measurements as its product, which is a legitimate outcome for a P1 -- 0008 already refuted the framing that made it a P1 (that it gates WI-kabif's removal arm)."  # a8b2
