- op: discuss  # 68c6
  at: '2026-09-02T03:03:29Z'  # 68c6
  by: agent  # 68c6
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 68c6
  clock: 9  # 68c6
  nonce: 68c6  # 68c6
  message: "OWNER RULING 2026-09-01: OPTION 3 FOR NOW -- do not build §4a. The choice between option 2 (build §4a AND rework the ddg bypass) and leaving it unbuilt is DEFERRED, not decided, so this item stays open as that decision's home rather than closing wont_do.\n\nTHREE CHANGES RECORDED, each with its reason:\n\nSTATUS todo_hard -> todo_soft. Nothing is owed until the deferred decision is\ntaken. It is not wont_do because option 2 remains live.\n\nPRIORITY P1 -> P3. The P1 rationale was that §4a gates WI-kabif's removal arm.\nMeasurement 0008 refuted that (removal can act only on ; it is 0 in\nevery repository, 0 of 28 running walks, and reproduced today on jaeger). An\nitem keeps a P1 because of what it unblocks, and this one no longer unblocks it.\n\nisbefore WI-kabif REMOVED, and this is the structural consequence worth\ncatching. That edge encoded exactly the refuted premise -- '§4a must land before\n§3a can decide inclusion'. Left standing while this item is deferred, it would\nhave blocked a live P1 (WI-kabif) behind a deferred P3 on a dependency\nmeasurement 0008 already showed is not real. AGENTS.md reserves isbefore for\nREAL dependencies. WI-kabif remains gated behind INV-busis on its own terms;\nremoving this edge does not unblock it, it removes a FALSE blocker.\n\nWHAT WOULD REOPEN THIS, written down rather than left to memory, because a\ndeferral with no trigger is just an item nobody looks at again:\n  * A measurement showing  is NOT ~0 among walks that composition\n    makes run. That is this item's own load-bearing unmeasured claim, it is\n    inferred from a base of 28, and it is the one result that would restore the\n    refutation payoff and with it the P1 case. Measuring it needs a throwaway\n    param_to_calls prototype -- no longer blocked by anything, since 0011 priced\n    the cost the item said had to be priced first.\n  * A decision to revisit the collapse key for reasons of its own. If INV-karud's\n     bypass is re-opened for any reason, option 2's marginal cost drops to\n    roughly the §4a build alone and the trade changes.\n  * Useful precision moving materially off 0006's 21.4%. The strongest argument\n    against building is that §3a is CONFIRM-ONLY, so composition adds confidence\n    to a population that is 78.6% not-useful -- a more confident false positive\n    is worse output, not better. If that base rate improves, so does the case.\n\nWHAT THIS ITEM PRODUCED, so the record does not read as abandonment: two\nmeasurements. 0008 (the ceiling, and the refutation of its own P1 framing) and\n0011 (the row price, the denominator correction, and the finding that §4a would\ninvalidate a premise the collapse design states quantitatively -- ddg at 1.43%\ntoday, 13.17% at the ceiling). A P1 that ends in two measurements and a refuted\npremise is a legitimate outcome, not a failure to deliver."  # 68c6
