  message: "CORRECTION to the preceding entry: three backticked terms were eaten by shell\ncommand-substitution when that note was posted (the tracker stored what bash\nhanded it). Edit-mode is human-gated, so the repair is here rather than in\nplace. The three damaged sentences read, in full:\n\n  * \"Measurement 0008 refuted that (removal can act only on `unconfirmed`; it\n    is 0 in every repository, 0 of 28 running walks, and reproduced today on\n    jaeger).\"\n\n  * \"A measurement showing `unconfirmed` is NOT ~0 among walks that composition\n    makes run.\"\n\n  * \"If INV-karud's `ddg` bypass is re-opened for any reason, option 2's\n    marginal cost drops to roughly the §4a build alone and the trade changes.\"\n\nNothing else in that entry was affected -- the loss is exactly the three words\n`unconfirmed` (twice) and `ddg` (once), each of which had been the subject of\nits sentence, which is why the sentences read as broken rather than merely\nwrong."  # 6ac2
