  message: "CONSUMER RECORDED, 2026-09-06 (WI-baran): tmux's sendmsg/recvmsg sites (compat/imsg-buffer.c) take the socket descriptor as a function PARAMETER; the AF_UNIX socket()/socketpair() calls are two functions up (client.c:122, server.c:123, proc.c:364). The same-function stamp abstains there, so measurement 0012's tmux VACUOUS deduction survives WI-baran. A parameter-to-argument summary that carries io_target_kind from the caller's binding to the callee's parameter is what would move it -- the read-side twin of the shape INV-fumod (a) closed \"fixed in principle\" against this item."  # d130
